From b5cfb68dcd7d0d0352445428f791eaa103eb7fab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:48:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 248/280] WIP: ASoC: rockchip: rockchip_sai: Request TX DMA
 earlier

The TX DMA request level is 16 words per lane, which leaves about 41 us
of audio in each lane FIFO at 192 kHz with two 32-bit slots per lane.
Mainline pl330 restarts each cyclic period from its interrupt handler
and sometimes takes longer than that, so 8-channel 192 kHz playback,
the format used for HBR passthrough, underruns several times a second.
Each underrun stops the stream and is heard as a dropout.

Request DMA at 28 words instead. The FIFO is 32 words per lane and a
16-beat burst over four lanes adds four words to each, so this is the
highest level that cannot overflow and nearly doubles the headroom.
On RK3576 8-channel S16_LE at 192 kHz then plays without underruns.

Fixes: cc78d1eaabad ("ASoC: rockchip: add Serial Audio Interface (SAI) driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
index c303732c652d..8fbbe3c7d4d4 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
@@ -1155,7 +1155,7 @@ static int rockchip_sai_init_dai(struct rk_sai_dev *sai, struct resource *res,
 	}
 
 	regmap_update_bits(sai->regmap, SAI_DMACR, SAI_DMACR_TDL_MASK,
-			   SAI_DMACR_TDL(16));
+			   SAI_DMACR_TDL(28));
 	regmap_update_bits(sai->regmap, SAI_DMACR, SAI_DMACR_RDL_MASK,
 			   SAI_DMACR_RDL(16));
 
